From 21fe54205e83a906a109cf294800e04f5d39bbb6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sathishkumar Muruganandam <murugana@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Fri, 18 Jul 2025 17:34:47 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath12k: handle empty failed regulatory events

Some QCN9274 firmware versions send a regulatory event with no rules when
the requested country cannot be applied.  The parser currently treats that
event as malformed before looking at the firmware status, and the caller
then executes an unconditional WARN_ON().  Keep the existing regulatory
domain for failed updates and avoid warning from the WMI receive path.

Based-on: 21fe54205e83a906a109cf294800e04f5d39bbb6
Link: https://git.codelinaro.org/clo/qsdk/oss/system/feeds/wlan-open/-/blob/1ee3a4ab7c59ceaff347c4668fc6c7604a04c323/patches/ath12k/0441-UPSTREAM-CP-wifi-ath12k-handle-invalid-country-in-reg-chanlist-ext-event.patch
Signed-off-by: Sathishkumar Muruganandam <murugana@qti.qualcomm.com>
Assisted-by: Codex:GPT-5.6-sol
Signed-off-by: Yanghan Ye <yyh94306@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/wmi.c | 15 +++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/wmi.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/wmi.c
@@ -5823,5 +5823,16 @@ static int ath12k_pull_reg_chan_list_ext
 
+	/* Preserve the firmware status before validating the rule count. */
+	reg_info->status_code = le32_to_cpu(ev->status_code);
+	reg_info->phy_id = le32_to_cpu(ev->phy_id);
+
 	if (!total_reg_rules) {
+		if (reg_info->status_code != REG_SET_CC_STATUS_PASS) {
+			ath12k_dbg(ab, ATH12K_DBG_REG,
+				   "ignoring empty regulatory event with status %u\n",
+				   reg_info->status_code);
+			kfree(tb);
+			return 0;
+		}
 		ath12k_warn(ab, "No reg rules available\n");
 		kfree(tb);
 		return -EINVAL;
@@ -6836,6 +6847,7 @@ fallback:
 	 * reverted at the fw and the old SCAN_CHAN_LIST cmd needs to be sent.
 	 */
 	/* TODO: This is rare, but still should also be handled */
-	WARN_ON(1);
+	ath12k_warn(ab,
+		   "failed to process regulatory event, retaining previous settings\n");
 
 out:
 	/* In some error cases, even a valid pdev_idx might not be available */
-- 
